sequenceDiagram
  title One representative, two cards: Edu keeps YSY's room and goes out (SDK run, examples/traces/dual-role.mjs, 10/10 checks)
  participant F as Fen's agent (no card)
  participant M as Maru's representative
  participant R as YSY's meeting room (Edu at the door, card 1)
  participant E as Edu going out (card 2)
  participant T as A tea shop
  participant Y as YSY (owner)
  Note over R,E: Same representative key (Edu). Card 1 and card 2 both signed by YSY's key.
  F->>R: greeting, unsigned
  R-->>F: greeting, lobby_briefing (the leaflet), not now, farewell
  M->>R: greeting, card_presentation
  R-->>M: card 1 with possession proof: Maru's representative checks it against the listing
  M->>R: introduction (vouch null), invitation_request: room.look, room.post
  R-->>M: grant: seated
  M->>R: act room.post
  E->>T: greeting, card_presentation (card 2 only: the shop never sees card 1)
  E->>T: introduction, invitation_request: purchase up to 15.00 USD
  T-->>E: grant: seated
  E->>T: act menu.view, act order.place 12.00 USD
  T-->>E: act_result ok, ok
  Y->>T: card_revocation of card 2 (delivered in a new visit of Edu's)
  E->>T: act menu.view on the old seat
  T-->>E: act_decision deny: the seat ended with its card (C198)
  M->>R: a new visit
  R-->>M: grant: card 1 untouched, the room stays open
